    "result_text": "Each claim now shows its status log, and all 4 tests in `bin/e2e` pass.\n\nEach line reads `<STATUS> by <user> on <date> due=<due>`, oldest first, in a new \"Status log\" column. Every line carries `data-testid=\"claim-log-line\"`, inside a list tagged `claim-log`.\n\n**Stored data**\n- New table `claim_status_log`, added in `V31__claim_status_log.sql`. Each row holds the status, who made the change, the sheet's today, and the due as text.\n- `Claim` has a `statusLog` list made of `StatusLogLine` entries. It is loaded with the claim.\n- Claims that already existed have no log. That doesn't matter today because the database is in-memory and starts empty on every run.\n\n**Server**\n- In `ClaimService`, a line is written when a claim is added (the DRAFT line) and on every status change: open, settle, PENDING, void, approve and reject. Batch \"open all\" also writes lines, because it goes through the same code.\n- Moving a claim to another person isn't a status change, so it writes no line.\n- The due is taken right after the change, using the same calculation as the rest of the app. A settled claim shows the figure it was settled at, and a claim with no rate shows `n/a`.\n- `ClaimView` returns the log in a new `statusLog` field.\n\n**Front end:** the new `statusLog` field is added to the `Claim` type in `claims-api.ts`, and the column is added in `claims.ts`.\n\nOne decision you might want to check: when a void or reject removes a late charge, the line records the due after the change, not before. The request didn't say which, and none of the tests cover that case. Switching to the before-figure is a small change if you want it.",
